<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aventicum</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Avenches</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aventicum was the capital of the Helvetii under Roman rule, on the site of the modern town of Avenches in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, near Lake Murten. Raised to a colony by Vespasian, it had walls more than 5 km long, an amphitheatre, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> and temples, and perhaps some 20,000 inhabitants. It declined after the Alemannic raids of the 3rd century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aventicum.jpg" alt="Aventicum" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (sidonius 16:58, 16 July 2006 (UTC)) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historische_Karte_CH_Rome_1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
